<title>MEXICO: Mexico workers' profit-sharing to remain at 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Mexico workers' profit-sharing to remain at 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican government said on Tuesday that the percentage of company profits to be shared among workers would remain at 10 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The resolution...adopted by the representatives of the labour, management and government sectors, ratifies the current percentage of 10 percent as the share of workers in the profits of companies,&quot; President Ernesto Zedillo's office said in a statement.</p>
<p>Zedillo signed the resolution, drawn up by the National Commission for Company Profit-sharing with Workers, in a ceremony at his official residence.</p>
<p>-- Martin Langfield, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559</p>
</text>
